{"package":"sklearn","sourceUrl":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/objects.inv","generatedAt":"2026-09-18T08:23:05.871Z","entries":[{"path":"sklearn.exceptions","kind":"module","dispname":"exceptions","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/api/sklearn.exceptions.html#module-sklearn.exceptions","signature":null,"doc":"Custom warnings and errors used across scikit-learn.","doc_summary":"Custom warnings and errors used across scikit-learn."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.ConvergenceWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"ConvergenceWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.ConvergenceWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.ConvergenceWarning","signature":"(...)","doc":"Custom warning to capture convergence problems\n\n.. versionchanged:: 0.18\n   Moved from sklearn.utils.","doc_summary":"Custom warning to capture convergence problems"},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.DataConversionWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"DataConversionWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.DataConversionWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.DataConversionWarning","signature":"(...)","doc":"Warning used to notify implicit data conversions happening in the code.\n\nThis warning occurs when some input data needs to be converted or\ninterpreted in a way that may not match the user's expectations.\n\nFor example, this warning may occur when the user\n    - passes an integer array to a function which expects float input and\n      will convert the input\n    - requests a non-copying operation, but a copy is required to meet the\n      implementation's data-type expectations;\n    - passes an input whose shape can be interpreted ambiguously.\n\n.. versionchanged:: 0.18\n   Moved from sklearn.utils.validation.","doc_summary":"Warning used to notify implicit data conversions happening in the code."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.DataDimensionalityWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"DataDimensionalityWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.DataDimensionalityWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.DataDimensionalityWarning","signature":"(...)","doc":"Custom warning to notify potential issues with data dimensionality.\n\nFor example, in random projection, this warning is raised when the\nnumber of components, which quantifies the dimensionality of the target\nprojection space, is higher than the number of features, which quantifies\nthe dimensionality of the original source space, to imply that the\ndimensionality of the problem will not be reduced.\n\n.. versionchanged:: 0.18\n   Moved from sklearn.utils.","doc_summary":"Custom warning to notify potential issues with data dimensionality."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.EfficiencyWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"EfficiencyWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.EfficiencyWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.EfficiencyWarning","signature":"(...)","doc":"Warning used to notify the user of inefficient computation.\n\nThis warning notifies the user that the efficiency may not be optimal due\nto some reason which may be included as a part of the warning message.\nThis may be subclassed into a more specific Warning class.\n\n.. versionadded:: 0.18","doc_summary":"Warning used to notify the user of inefficient computation."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.EstimatorCheckFailedWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"EstimatorCheckFailedWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.EstimatorCheckFailedWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.EstimatorCheckFailedWarning","signature":"(*, estimator, check_name: str, exception: Exception, status: str, expected_to_fail: bool, expected_to_fail_reason: str)","doc":"Warning raised when an estimator check from the common tests fails.\n\nParameters\n----------\nestimator : estimator object\n    Estimator instance for which the test failed.\n\ncheck_name : str\n    Name of the check that failed.\n\nexception : Exception\n    Exception raised by the failed check.\n\nstatus : str\n    Status of the check.\n\nexpected_to_fail : bool\n    Whether the check was expected to fail.\n\nexpected_to_fail_reason : str\n    Reason for the expected failure.","doc_summary":"Warning raised when an estimator check from the common tests fails."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.FitFailedWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"FitFailedWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.FitFailedWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.FitFailedWarning","signature":"(...)","doc":"Warning class used if there is an error while fitting the estimator.\n\nThis Warning is used in meta estimators GridSearchCV and RandomizedSearchCV\nand the cross-validation helper function cross_val_score to warn when there\nis an error while fitting the estimator.\n\n.. versionchanged:: 0.18\n   Moved from sklearn.cross_validation.","doc_summary":"Warning class used if there is an error while fitting the estimator."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.InconsistentVersionWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"InconsistentVersionWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.InconsistentVersionWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.InconsistentVersionWarning","signature":"(*, estimator_name, current_sklearn_version, original_sklearn_version)","doc":"Warning raised when an estimator is unpickled with an inconsistent version.\n\nParameters\n----------\nestimator_name : str\n    Estimator name.\n\ncurrent_sklearn_version : str\n    Current scikit-learn version.\n\noriginal_sklearn_version : str\n    Original scikit-learn version.","doc_summary":"Warning raised when an estimator is unpickled with an inconsistent version."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.NotFittedError","kind":"class","dispname":"NotFittedError","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.NotFittedError.html#sklearn.exceptions.NotFittedError","signature":"(...)","doc":"Exception class to raise if estimator is used before fitting.\n\nThis class inherits from both ValueError and AttributeError to help with\nexception handling and backward compatibility.\n\nExamples\n--------\n>>> from sklearn.svm import LinearSVC\n>>> from sklearn.exceptions import NotFittedError\n>>> try:\n...     LinearSVC().predict([[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4]])\n... except NotFittedError as e:\n...     print(repr(e))\nNotFittedError(\"This LinearSVC instance is not fitted yet. Call 'fit' with\nappropriate arguments before using this estimator.\"...)\n\n.. versionchanged:: 0.18\n   Moved from sklearn.utils.validation.","doc_summary":"Exception class to raise if estimator is used before fitting."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.UndefinedMetricWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"UndefinedMetricWarning","docUri":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.exceptions.UndefinedMetricWarning.html#sklearn.exceptions.UndefinedMetricWarning","signature":"(...)","doc":"Warning used when the metric is invalid\n\n.. versionchanged:: 0.18\n   Moved from sklearn.base.","doc_summary":"Warning used when the metric is invalid"},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.PositiveSpectrumWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"PositiveSpectrumWarning","docUri":null,"signature":"(...)","doc":"Warning raised when the eigenvalues of a PSD matrix have issues\n\nThis warning is typically raised by ``_check_psd_eigenvalues`` when the\neigenvalues of a positive semidefinite (PSD) matrix such as a gram matrix\n(kernel) present significant negative eigenvalues, or bad conditioning i.e.\nvery small non-zero eigenvalues compared to the largest eigenvalue.\n\n.. versionadded:: 0.22","doc_summary":"Warning raised when the eigenvalues of a PSD matrix have issues"},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.SkipTestWarning","kind":"class","dispname":"SkipTestWarning","docUri":null,"signature":"(...)","doc":"Warning class used to notify the user of a test that was skipped.\n\nFor example, one of the estimator checks requires a pandas import.\nIf the pandas package cannot be imported, the test will be skipped rather\nthan register as a failure.","doc_summary":"Warning class used to notify the user of a test that was skipped."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.UnsetMetadataPassedError","kind":"class","dispname":"UnsetMetadataPassedError","docUri":null,"signature":"(*, message, unrequested_params, routed_params)","doc":"Exception class to raise if a metadata is passed which is not explicitly         requested (metadata=True) or not requested (metadata=False).\n\n.. versionadded:: 1.3\n\nParameters\n----------\nmessage : str\n    The message\n\nunrequested_params : dict\n    A dictionary of parameters and their values which are provided but not\n    requested.\n\nrouted_params : dict\n    A dictionary of routed parameters.","doc_summary":"Exception class to raise if a metadata is passed which is not explicitly         requested (metadata=True) or not requested (metadata=False)."},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__all__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__all__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__builtins__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__builtins__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__cached__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__cached__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__doc__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__doc__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__file__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__file__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__loader__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__loader__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__name__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__name__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__package__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__package__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.__spec__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__spec__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"sklearn.exceptions.Co